{"assessments":[{"claim":"H7","status":"accept","investigation":"closed","evidence":["R7","R26"]}],"proposals":[{"outcome":"dependency_composite","exposure":"tp53_loss","exposed":1.0,"comparator":0.0,"contrast":"mean_difference","eligibility":[{"variable":"keap1_loss","op":"eq","value":0.0},{"variable":"smarca4_loss","op":"eq","value":0.0}],"subgroup":[],"direction":1,"anticipated_direction":1,"initial_status":"unresolved","parent":"H15"},{"outcome":"dependency_composite","exposure":"smarca4_loss","exposed":1.0,"comparator":0.0,"contrast":"mean_difference","eligibility":[{"variable":"tp53_loss","op":"eq","value":0.0},{"variable":"keap1_loss","op":"eq","value":0.0}],"subgroup":[],"direction":-1,"anticipated_direction":-1,"initial_status":"unresolved","parent":"H13"},{"outcome":"dependency_composite","exposure":"keap1_loss","exposed":1.0,"comparator":0.0,"contrast":"mean_difference","eligibility":[{"variable":"tp53_loss","op":"eq","value":0.0},{"variable":"smarca4_loss","op":"eq","value":0.0}],"subgroup":[],"direction":1,"anticipated_direction":1,"initial_status":"unresolved","parent":"H14"}],"research_notes":"Validated accepted main dataset associations: TP53 loss -> higher dependency_composite/weaker dependency (H3, +0.423 [0.327,0.520]); SMARCA4 loss -> lower composite/stronger dependency (H5 discovery +0.833 [0.767,0.898], validation +0.795 [0.695,0.896]); KEAP1 loss -> higher composite/weaker dependency (H7 discovery +0.832 [0.766,0.897], validation +0.783 [0.688,0.878]). Conditional effects remain large when each predictor is fixed to remove the others, and SMARCA4-by-KEAP1 interactions are near zero (H25/H26 rejected), supporting separable dataset associations rather than one absorbing the other. Negative closed findings: lineage subtype, KRAS main effect, MTAP loss, PIK3CA mutation, MYC amplification, marker D/E/F main effects, KRAS x marker D. Next priorities: (1) run new double-negative conditional claims to test residual effects when both other strong predictors are absent; (2) run TP53 interactions with SMARCA4 and KEAP1 (H27/H28); (3) run remaining driver screens H18-H22; (4) run technical audits H23/H33-H35. These remain dataset associations, not causal claims or broader generalizability claims.","narrative":"The independent validation for H7 KEAP1 loss supports the discovery result. The discovery mean difference was +0.832 composite units with 95% CI +0.766 to +0.897; the independent validation estimate was +0.783 with interval +0.688 to +0.878 under the stricter validation alpha. Both estimates are far above the 0.15-unit effect-size threshold in the claimed positive direction. Because more negative dependency_composite values mean stronger dependency and the claim direction is positive, KEAP1 loss is associated with a higher composite score, i.e., weaker measured dependency. The validation interval remains well above zero and above the scientific threshold, so H7 stays accepted and can be considered closed for the main effect.

This validation strengthens the current core dataset findings. We now have independent support for SMARCA4 loss (stronger dependency, lower composite) and KEAP1 loss (weaker dependency, higher composite). TP53 loss remains accepted but not independently validated; its discovery estimate is smaller but still robust. The conditional analyses show that SMARCA4 and KEAP1 effects remain large when the other predictor is absent or present, while the formal SMARCA4-by-KEAP1 interactions are negligible, arguing against a simple overlap/confounding explanation for either main effect within this dataset.

The next most informative analyses are the new double-negative conditional claims: the effect of each strong predictor in lines lacking the other two strong predictors. If all three remain above threshold there, the dataset supports highly separable main effects. I will also run the already registered TP53 interactions with SMARCA4 and KEAP1, the remaining tumor-suppressor/driver screens, and technical audits. Technical audits are important because a large shift associated with CRISPR library or matched-omics status would caution that observed associations may reflect processing strata, though they still would not establish causality."}
